[2025-12-15 13:59:03,428: WARNING/ForkPoolWorker-3] [LLM] ✓ Summary generated using: ChatCompletion(id='chatcmpl-Cn2S6sGUUexCWjIy8XwMmHDatLQ6K', choices=[Choice(finish_reason='stop', index=0, logprobs=None, message=ChatCompletionMessage(content='# Summary of Clinical Trials Related to Breast Cancer\n\nThis summary consolidates key findings from 10 clinical trials related to breast cancer, categorized by trial phase and status, with practical insights for researchers, clinicians, and patients.\n\n---\n\n## Trials by Phase and Status\n\n### Phase 1 Trials\n- **Completed**\n  - [NCT03663881](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03663881): Safety assessment of P2Et extract in healthy volunteers (Colombia). Focus on toxicity and safety issues.  \n    *Start Date:* April 2019\n- **Unknown Status**\n  - [NCT05755581](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05755581): Efficacy of neoadjuvant endocrine therapy vs chemotherapy in female breast cancer patients.  \n    *Start Date:* April 2023\n- **Terminated**\n  - [NCT01596530](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01596530): Evaluation of drug activity in women with breast cancer without prior Herceptin treatment.  \n    *Start Date:* June 2012\n\n### Phase 2 Trials\n- **Active, Not Recruiting**\n  - [NCT06033092](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT06033092): Low dose Tamoxifen combined with lifestyle changes for breast cancer prevention targeting BRCA and PALB2 mutation carriers and ductal carcinoma in situ.  \n    *Start Date:* June 2024\n\n### Phase 4 Trials\n- **Completed**\n  - [NCT04827030](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT04827030): ER-One trial comparing erector spinae block (ESP) versus paravertebral block (PVB) for pain management before breast cancer surgery.  \n    *Start Date:* June 2021\n\n---\n\n## Trials by Study Type and Status\n\n### Interventional Trials\n- **Completed**\n  - [NCT03663881](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03663881): Safety of P2Et extract (Phase 1)  \n  - [NCT03981666](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT03981666): Video-based cognitive behavioral therapy for insomnia in adult cancer patients and survivors (non-phase specific)  \n  - [NCT04827030](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT04827030): Pain block comparison before surgery (Phase 4)  \n  - [NCT02619292](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT02619292): Mindful movement intervention for breast cancer survivors (non-phase specific)  \n- **Unknown Status**\n  - [NCT05240937](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05240937): Effect of self-compassion on breast cancer outcomes (non-phase specific)  \n  - [NCT05755581](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT05755581): Neoadjuvant endocrine therapy vs chemotherapy efficacy (Phase 1)  \n- **Terminated**\n  - [NCT01596530](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01596530): Drug activity evaluation without prior Herceptin (Phase 1)  \n- **Active, Not Recruiting**\n  - [NCT06033092](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT06033092): Low dose Tamoxifen and lifestyle changes for prevention (Phase 2)  \n\n### Observational Trials\n- **Not Yet Recruiting**\n  - [NCT06238453](https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT06238453): Effect of WhatsApp-based training on mammography health beliefs and behaviors in breast cancer context.  \n    *Start Date:* February 2024\n\n---\n\n## Practical Insights\n\n- **Emerging Therapies & Prevention:** Phase 1 and 2 trials are investigating new therapeutic approaches, including neoadjuvant endocrine therapy and low-dose Tamoxifen combined with lifestyle modifications for prevention, especially in genetically predisposed populations.\n- **Supportive Care:** Completed trials highlight interventions addressing quality of life issues such as insomnia (cognitive behavioral therapy) and pain management during surgery (nerve blocks), as well as mindful movement for survivors.\n- **Patient Education & Behavior:** Upcoming observational studies aim to leverage digital platforms (e.g., WhatsApp) to improve mammography uptake and health beliefs, indicating a trend towards integrating technology in patient engagement.\n- **Trial Status Awareness:** Several trials have unknown or terminated status, underscoring the importance of verifying current trial availability and enrollment status before considering participation.\n\n---\n\nThis overview aids stakeholders in identifying ongoing and completed research areas in breast cancer, facilitating informed decisions regarding clinical trial involvement and emerging treatment or supportive care options.', refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=None))], created=1765803534, model='gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14', object='chat.completion', service_tier='default', system_fingerprint='fp_d0c93c37b1', usage=CompletionUsage(completion_tokens=977, prompt_tokens=1272, total_tokens=2249, completion_tokens_details=CompletionTokensDetails(accepted_prediction_tokens=0, audio_tokens=0, reasoning_tokens=0, rejected_prediction_tokens=0), prompt_tokens_details=PromptTokensDetails(audio_tokens=0, cached_tokens=0)))
