e: October 2019  \n\n- **NCT04037852**  \n  *Robotic vs Conventional/Endoscopic Nipple Sparing Mastectomy*  \n  - Objective: Compare surgical approaches in breast cancer management  \n  - Start Date: October 2019  \n\n- **NCT05703269**  \n  *Single vs Multiple Dose Radiation in Patients with Brain Metastases Receiving Immunotherapy*  \n  - Includes breast carcinoma among other cancers  \n  - Start Date: July 2023  \n\n- **NCT05190978**  \n  *Randomized Feasibility Trial for Mesh in Pre-Pectoral Reconstruction*  \n  - Focus: Breast reconstruction complications and infection prevention  \n  - Start Date: October 2022  \n\n- **NCT05656716**  \n  *Multimodal Project*  \n  - Focus: Breast cancer (details not specified)  \n  - Start Date: January 2023  \n\n---\n\n## Interventional Studies Focused on Supportive Care and Survivorship\n\n- **NCT06855654**  \n  *Promoting Resilience in Women with Breast Cancer (PRISM-MBC)*  \n  - Aim: Psychological resilience enhancement for metastatic breast cancer patients  \n  - Start Date: January 2025  \n\n- **NCT05930483**  \n  *Remotely Delivered, Community-Aligned Weight Loss Interventions Among Breast Cancer Survivors (¡Vida! Trial)*  \n  - Target: Stage I-III breast cancer survivors  \n  - Start Date: April 2025  \n\n- **NCT05146297**  \n  *Diversity and Inclusion in Research Underpinning Prevention and Therapy Trials*  \n  - Includes breast cancer among other cancers  \n  - Start Date: April 2023  \n\n- **NCT03509090**  \n  *Erector Spinae Block in Segmental Mastectomy*  \n  - Status: Unknown  \n  - Start Date: April 2018  \n\n---\n\n## Observational Studies\n\n- **NCT06939049**  \n  *Development of New Methodologies and Innovative Tools for Diagnosis and Treatment*  \n  - Focus: Cancer risk including breast cancer  \n  - Start Date: May 2017  \n\n- **NCT04888351**  \n  *Immediate Breast Reconstruction's Increasing*  \n  - Focus: Trends and outcomes in breast reconstruction  \n  - Start Date: January 2021  \n\n- **NCT04587258**  \n  *Improving Cancer Screening and Prevention During COVID-19 in Underserved Populations*  \n  - Includes breast cancer screening  \n  - Status: Unknown  \n  - Start Date: August 2020  \n\n- **NCT03987633**  \n  *EMPOWER-1: Reducing Health Inequality*  \n  - Broader cardiovascular and cancer focus, recruiting status active  \n  - Start Date: February 2020  \n\n- **NCT03400514**  \n  *Clinical Concordance Study Between Watson for Oncology and Clinician Practice*  \n  - Focus: AI in cancer treatment decision-making  \n  - Status: Unknown  \n  - Start Date: April 2017  \n\n---\n\n## Practical Insights\n\n- **Patient Eligibility:** Many trials focus on early-stage breast cancer (Stage I-III), hormone receptor status, and specific subtypes such as triple-negative breast cancer.  \n- **Emerging Technologies:** Mobile health ultrasound and robotic surgery trials indicate growing integration of technology in diagnosis and surgical management.  \n- **Supportive Care:** Trials on fatigue management, resilience, and weight loss highlight the emphasis on survivorship quality of life.  \n- **Diversity and Inclusion:** Ongoing efforts to improve representation in research suggest opportunities for underrepresented populations to participate.  \n- **Trial Access:** Most trials are recruiting and based in the USA, with some starting as early as 2017 and others planned through 2025, offering a range of enrollment opportunities.\n\n---\n\n**For clinicians and patients seeking trial participation, reviewing eligibility criteria and trial locations via the provided ClinicalTrials.gov links is recommended to identify suitable options.**", refusal=None, role='assistant', annotations=[], audio=None, function_call=None, tool_calls=None))], created=1765803543, model='gpt-4.1-mini-2025-04-14', object='chat.completion', service_tier='default', system_fingerprint='fp_d0c93c37b1', usage=CompletionUsage(completion_tokens=1237, prompt_tokens=2085, total_tokens=3322, completion_tokens_details=Compl